---
import LegalShell from '../components/LegalShell.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalShell
  title="Cookie Notice — Basebond Solutions"
  heading="Cookie Notice"
  updated="21 November 2026"
  path="/cookies"
  description="What cookies and similar technologies this website uses, and how to control them."
  intro="This notice explains the small amount of browser storage this site uses, and how you can control it."
>
  <h2>1. What this site uses</h2>
  <p>
    This website does not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels or third-party
    marketing cookies. It does not build a profile of you across other websites.
  </p>
  <p>The only browser storage used is:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Essential functionality</strong> — nothing beyond what the browser needs to display the site and submit a form.</li>
    <li><strong>Local fonts and styles</strong> — typography and styles are served from this domain, so no font provider receives your IP address.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    If we add website analytics, we will use a cookieless, privacy-respecting service that
    does not set identifying cookies. If that changes to anything that does set cookies,
    this notice will be updated and consent will be requested before any non-essential
    cookie is placed.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Third-party services you choose to use</h2>
  <p>
    Clicking a WhatsApp link opens WhatsApp, which is operated by a third party and has
    its own privacy and cookie practices. The same applies to any external site we link
    to. We do not control those practices.
  </p>

  <h2>4. How to control cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can clear or block cookies and site data in your browser settings. Because this
    site does not rely on cookies for functionality, blocking them will not affect your
    ability to use it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Questions</h2>
  <p>
    For anything relating to this notice, contact
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Our wider handling of personal
    information is described in the <a href="/privacy">privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
</LegalShell>
